My current skincare routine that works for my dry & sensitive skin ✨🤍

A lot of you have been asking for an updated skincare routine, especially after the skin reaction I experienced earlier this year that seemed to stick around for months. While I’m still learning what works best for my skin, these are the products I’ve been consistently using and loving when my skin is happy and healthy:

@elemis Pro-Collagen Cleansing Balm
@officialvanicream Gentle Facial Cleanser
@paulaschoice Skin Perfecting 2% BHA Liquid Exfoliant
@anua_global Azelaic Acid 10 Hyaluron Redness Soothing Serum
@larocheposay Cicaplast Baume B5+
@aestura_ca Atobarrier 365 Cream
@tower28beauty SOS Daily Rescue Facial Spray
@neutrogenacanada Hydro Boost Lip Oil

One thing I’ve learned over the past 6–7 months is that skincare is only one piece of the puzzle. I’ve noticed that I tend to break out about a week before my cycle, when I’m dehydrated, when I’m eating a lot of processed foods, and when I’m not staying on top of things like washing my makeup brushes and changing my pillowcases regularly.

When my skin is reacting, I actually simplify everything and stick mostly to moisturizer until my skin calms down before slowly reintroducing products again.

Most importantly: what works for me may not work for you. Every product above was introduced one at a time, and I always patch tested before making it part of my routine.

If you’re currently struggling with skin reactions or breakouts that are affecting your confidence, you’re not alone. Be patient with yourself, give your skin time, and don’t be afraid to seek professional advice if needed 🤍

